event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/plan.md\", \"content\": \"Plan for mission \\\"greet, tested\\\":\\n\\n1. Send dev a dispatch (d1) asking it to implement src/greet.py with\\n   greet(name) -\u003e \\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\" and tests/test_greet.py covering a normal\\n   name and the empty string, verify with `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`\\n   exiting 0, commit to its own branch, and reply honestly.\\n2. Wait for dev's reply.\\n3. Judge: fetch dev's branch, inspect src/greet.py and tests/test_greet.py,\\n   run `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` myself against the fetched\\n   tree to confirm exit code 0 and that both required cases are actually\\n   exercised (not just present but trivial/no-op).\\n4. If all three criteria hold (file+function, tests+both cases, suite exits\\n   0), accept dev's work and reply to mission m1 with --outcome campaign-met.\\n5. If something is missing or wrong, send dev a rework dispatch naming\\n   precisely what is unmet, and repeat from step 2.\\n6. This is a small mission — if it stalls (dev dead/wedged beyond wait's\\n   auto-recovery, or repeated rework not converging), wrap up honestly with\\n   campaign-converged/exhausted/blocked as appropriate rather than looping\\n   indefinitely.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

